-- hakawi:down reversibility=data-loss data-loss=columns reason=Drops the notification_preferences.messages column. Every stored user row has a value in it, because the forward migration filled the column for all of them, so a user who has since muted direct messages silently loses that choice and is told about messages again for as long as the column is gone. A dropped boolean is not reconstructible from what remains, which is why this is declared data loss rather than a reversible change; the prior state is not "a user who never configured messages" but "a user whose configuration of messages was erased".
ALTER TABLE notification_preferences DROP COLUMN IF EXISTS messages;